.TH CVECTOR_APPEND_CVECTOR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_append_cvector \- append a vector to a vector
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

bool cvector_append_cvector(cvec v_to, cvec v_from);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Appends every element of one vector to another. Both vectors must have the
same element size.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v_to    Destination vector
v_from  Source vector
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
true on success.
false when the combined element count overflows or is more than
ccol_max_elem_count, or when the memory allocation fails.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The two element sizes must match; the function asserts when they don't,
and also when v_to or v_from is NULL.

Either all the elements are appended or none are, and more capacity is
reserved automatically when needed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_append_cvec (3),
.BR cvector_append_array (3)
